        "paragraph_id": "299BC61E",
        "text": "In the Manning formulation the Manning coefficient (n) must be specified. The dimensionless friction coefficient is calculated from (2.49). Manning can be seen as a depth-dependent Chézy value and a typical Manning value for sandy coasts would be in the order of 0.02 s/m1/3."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 21677,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 615,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 523,
        "paragraph_id": "5A25A678",
        "text": "In the White-Colebrook formulation the geometrical roughness of Nikuradse (ks) must be specified. The dimensionless friction coefficient is calculated from (2.50) The White-Colebrook formulation has al log relation with the water depth and a typical ks value for sandy coasts would be in the order of 0.01 - 0.15 m."
      },
